.TH PRIME-AGENT 1 "October 2026" "Prime Agent" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prime-agent \- coding agent harness with a persistent Python control environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prime-agent
.RI [ options ] " [@files...] [message...]"
.br
.B prime-agent
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prime-agent
runs coding agents through a terminal interface, with persistent sessions,
a Python control environment, and bundled skills.
Without a command or a noninteractive mode, it opens the interactive interface.
.PP
Use
.B prime-agent --help
for the complete option and command list, and
.BI "prime-agent help " command
for command-specific help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -p ", " --print
Print a response and exit.
.TP
.BI --mode " text|json|rpc|acp|daemon"
Select an output mode. The default is text.
.TP
.BI --cwd " directory"
Use the specified working directory.
.TP
.B --offline
Disable startup network operations.
.TP
.BI --provider " name"
Select a model provider.
.TP
.BI --model " id"
Select a model.
.TP
.BR -c ", " --continue
Continue the previous session.
.TP
.BR -r ", " --resume " [path|id]"
Open the agents view, or resume the specified saved session.
.TP
.BI --session-dir " directory"
Use the specified session directory.
.TP
.B --no-session
Do not save the session.
.TP
.BI --skill " path"
Load a skill. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show command-line help.
.SH COMMANDS
.B agents
searches and opens sessions;
.B attach
attaches the interactive interface to an agent;
.B stop
stops an agent; and
.B send
sends a message to an agent.
.PP
.B model
inspects available models;
.B session
manages saved sessions;
.B mcp
manages user MCP servers; and
.B package
manages capability packages.
.PP
.B prompt
prints the assembled system prompt with its layer breakdown.
.B status
shows background service status.
.B doctor
inspects and safely cleans up background services.
.PP
Run
.B prime-agent --help
to list additional commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.prime/agent/sessions/
Saved session data.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/prime-agent/
The installed executable, bundled Python runtime sources, skills, and catalogs.
.SH NOTES
The Python kernel environment is provisioned by
.B uv
on first use. Install uv separately using the upstream installation method;
Prime Agent searches PATH and ~/.local/bin/uv.
If uv is missing, it prints installation guidance without running an installer.
Alternatively, set
.B PRIME_AGENT_KERNEL_PYTHON
to the interpreter in a prepared Python environment containing the current
runtime and its required packages.
Model access and runtime provisioning may require network access.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start an interactive session:
.PP
.nf
prime-agent
.fi
.PP
Print a response without opening the interactive interface:
.PP
.nf
prime-agent --print "Summarize this repository"
.fi
.PP
Continue the previous session:
.PP
.nf
prime-agent --continue
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B prime-agent --help
.br
.BI "prime-agent help " command
.PP
Project homepage: https://github.com/PrimeIntellect-ai/prime-agent
